.TH BLANKRES-GTK 1 "September 2026" "blankres 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
blankres-gtk \- review crash reports before they are sent
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B blankres-gtk
.SH DESCRIPTION
A desktop window for deciding what happens to a crash report.
.PP
The window opens only for crashes the crash server has actually asked for a full payload for, which
on a well-populated crash database is a small fraction of them. A core dump is a copy of the
crashed process's memory and may contain documents, keystrokes, session cookies or private keys, so
the window states its size in plain language and lists every field that would be transmitted.
Nothing is uploaded until
.B Send report
is pressed.
.PP
.B Never for this problem
records the crash signature in the user's own crash directory, which the daemon then honours.
.PP
Started automatically by a systemd user path unit when a report appears, and available from the
desktop menu as \(lqCrash Reporting\(rq.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BLANKRES_CONFIG
Configuration file to read instead of
.IR /etc/blankres/client.json .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR blankres (1),
.BR blankresd (8)
